Subject: [PATCH] sdio: retain the configured clock across card removal

esp_init_interface_layer() sets the requested clock once at module init.
esp_remove() clears the transport context, including that configuration,
so a later probe skips the clock override. On the Waveshare P4/C6 this
leaves the bus at the MMC-negotiated 20 MHz while clockspeed still says 5.

Keep the module-lifetime clock configuration when clearing per-card state.
The next probe can then apply the same requested rate before opening the
data path. Reset GPIO ownership and the transfer/queue paths are unchanged.

--- a/sdio/esp_sdio.c
+++ b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
@@ -645,6 +645,7 @@ static void esp_remove(struct sdio_func *func)
 {
 	struct esp_sdio_context *context;
 	uint8_t prio_q_idx = 0;
+	u32 sdio_clk_mhz;
 
 	context = sdio_get_drvdata(func);
 
@@ -683,7 +684,10 @@ static void esp_remove(struct sdio_func *func)
 			context->func = NULL;
 			context->adapter->dev = NULL;
 		}
+		/* The clock is configured at module init, not on each probe. */
+		sdio_clk_mhz = context->sdio_clk_mhz;
 		memset(context, 0, sizeof(struct esp_sdio_context));
+		context->sdio_clk_mhz = sdio_clk_mhz;
 	}
 	esp_dbg("ESP SDIO cleanup completed\n");
 }
